		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=16017&amp;sid=e54f1202f1299d3082712a73041d9873#16017"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Nov 05, 2002 7:33 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=16017&amp;sid=e54f1202f1299d3082712a73041d9873"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Marcelas walks by and sees the Gnome staring curiously at the locked door.  Understanding the look that he's seen so many times before, Marc pushes down the sign that is magically stuck to the door until it is low enough for the newcomer to read it.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
<i>Beyond this door lies the Hall of the Concordat Angelis.  All who belong to the guild, even Tyro's, are allowed to enter.  The door is locked with a magical phrase that each must protect with their life.  To receive this phrase, simply contact one of your fellow guildmates.  You can also send an </i> ... the next word is scribbled out and written over many times but the letters can still barely be made out ... <i> <b>e m a i l </b> to <a href="mailto:jimmy@pico-consulting.com">jimmy@pico-consulting.com</a> requesting the pass phrase.  This will also enroll you in the newsletter that is sent out to announce hunts and events.</i>
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
While the Gnome studies the note, Marc wanders off in the general direction of the beast known as The Work.  Those that he passes see a peculiar object in his hands emitting curious whirring, beeping, and humming noises.  There is also a piece of glass with ever changing letters flashing upon its surface.  Oddly, his hands fly over a flat panel with raised buttons almost as if he is enchanted by some strange and silent call from this machine. 
<br />
Marcelas Hiddenstrike
<br />

<br />
Scout of the Concordat
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />The good thing about repeating your mistakes is that you know when to duck.</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
